=============
## SCALING
=============

Scaling is the process of increasing the system's capacity to handle the increased workload.

---------------------------
WHY DO WE NEED SCALING ?
---------------------------

Sabse pehle ek simple E-commerce Spring Boot Application lete hain jo ek
single Physical Machine (PM) ya Virtual Machine (VM) par deployed hai.

Architecture:

             Users
                |
                |
                v
        ----------------
        | Spring Boot  |
        | Application  |
        ----------------
                |
                |
                v
             Database

Spring Boot application embedded application server (e.g. Tomcat) ke saath
isi Physical/Virtual server par run kar rahi hai.

Ab is server ke paas kuch limited resources hain.



## SERVER RESOURCES
---------------------

CPU              : 2 Cores
RAM              : 4 GB
Disk             : 100 GB
Network Card     : 1 Gbps



## APPLICATION RESOURCES
--------------------------

1: WORKER THREADS :
--------------------

Har incoming HTTP request ko process karne ke liye Tomcat ko ek worker thread
allocate karna padta hai.

Suppose Tomcat configuration:

    Maximum Threads = 200

Matlab Tomcat ke paas maximum 200 worker threads available hain request
processing ke liye.

Tomcat ek time par maximum 200 requests actively process kar sakta hai
(assuming each request occupies one worker thread).

Baaki requests:

    - Accept Queue me wait kar sakti hain
      (OS / Tomcat configuration par depend karta hai)

                OR

    - Overload hone par reject bhi ho sakti hain.



2: DATABASE CONNECTIONS :
-------------------------

Spring Boot application database se communicate karne ke liye
connection pool use karti hai.

Suppose configuration:

    Maximum Pool Size = 100

Matlab ek time par application maximum 100 active database connections
use kar sakti hai.



## INITIALLY EVERYTHING WORKS FINE :
------------------------------------

Suppose application ke sirf

    100 Users

hain.

Traffic bhi kam hai.

Server ke resources sufficient hain.

Application smoothly chal rahi hai.



## COMPANY STARTS GROWING :
---------------------------

Initially:

    Users

        100

Server Traffic

        10 Requests / Second

Server easily handle kar raha tha.


Kuch months baad:

    Users

        10,000

Ab naturally application par incoming HTTP requests bhi badhne lagti hain.

Suppose traffic increase hokar

    500 Requests / Second

ho gayi.

Server ab bhi kaam kar raha hai, lekin CPU utilization aur memory usage
increase hone lagi.


Aur kuch months baad:

    Users

        100,000

Suppose traffic aur badhkar

    2,000 Requests / Second

ho gayi.

Ab actual problems start hoti hain.



## WHAT EXACTLY STARTS FAILING ?
----------------------------------


1. CPU BECOMES A BOTTLENECK
------------------------------

Har incoming HTTP request ko process karne ke liye ek worker thread allocate
hota hai aur wo thread CPU instructions execute karta hai.

Initially:

    Traffic

        10 Requests / Second

    CPU Utilization

        15%

Traffic increase hua:

    Traffic

        500 Requests / Second

    CPU Utilization

        75%

Traffic aur badha:

    Traffic

        2,000 Requests / Second

    CPU Utilization

        100%

Ab CPU continuously busy hai.

Naye requests ko process karne ke liye immediately CPU time available nahi hai.

Result:

    Response Time increase hone lagta hai.

    Latency badhne lagti hai.



2. TOMCAT THREADS GET EXHAUSTED
----------------------------------

Suppose:

    Tomcat Worker Threads = 200

Ek request ko complete hone me

    2 Seconds

lag rahe hain.

Agar ek hi time par

    500 Requests

aa jaati hain,

to kya hoga?

Pehli

    200 Requests

ko worker thread mil jayega.

Baaki

    300 Requests

immediately process nahi ho paayengi.

Wo:

    - Accept Queue me wait karengi
      (agar queue me jagah hai)

                OR

    - Queue bhi full ho gayi to reject ho sakti hain.


## RESULT:
-----------

    High Response Time
            ↓
        Timeouts
            ↓
    5xx Errors (depending on situation)



3. DATABASE CONNECTION POOL GETS EXHAUSTED
---------------------------------------------

Suppose:

    Maximum DB Connections = 100

Ab ek hi time par

    300 Requests

database access karna chahti hain.

Kya application

    300

database connections bana legi?

Nahi.

Sirf

    100

connections available hain.

Baaki requests connection available hone ka wait karengi.

Agar bahut der tak connection available nahi hua,

to request fail bhi ho sakti hai.


## RESULT :
------------

    Slow Queries
            ↓
        Waiting
            ↓
    Connection Timeout



4. RAM STARTS FILLING UP
--------------------------

Har request kuch memory consume karti hai.

Example:

    - Request Objects
    - Response Objects
    - Local Variables
    - JSON Serialization
    - Hibernate Objects
    - Session Data

Initially:

    RAM Usage

        1 GB / 4 GB

Traffic badha:

    RAM Usage

        3.5 GB / 4 GB

Aur badha:

    RAM Usage

        4 GB / 4 GB

Ab JVM ko Garbage Collection frequently run karni padegi.

GC jab memory reclaim karti hai, kuch phases me application threads ko temporarily stop karna pad sakta hai.

Agar memory fir bhi insufficient hui,

to application

    OutOfMemoryError

bhi throw kar sakti hai.



5. NETWORK BANDWIDTH ALSO HAS A LIMIT
----------------------------------------

Suppose server ka Network Interface Card support karta hai

    1 Gbps

Lekin incoming + outgoing traffic ho gaya

    3 Gbps

Impossible.

Network packets queue hone lagenge.

Result:

    Latency increase hogi.

    Throughput degrade hoga.



## FINAL OBSERVATION
---------------------

Ab dhyan se dekho.

Application me koi bug nahi aaya.

Problem sirf itni hai ki

    Existing Workload

            >

    Server Capacity

ho gayi hai.



## WHAT IS THE ROOT CAUSE ?
----------------------------

Root Cause:

Ek single machine ke resources finite (limited) hote hain.

Chahe wo:

    - CPU
    - RAM
    - Network
    - Thread Pool
    - Database Connections

In sab ki ek upper limit hoti hai.

Jaise-jaise traffic increase hota hai,

ye resources gradually saturate hone lagte hain.



Q1. CAN AN APPLICATION BECOME SLOW EVEN IF APPLICATION SERVER CPU USAGE IS ONLY 20% ?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Yes. It is possible , slow database could possibly be the potential reason behind the same.


Suppose Tomcat ke paas:

    200 Worker Threads

Aur DB Connection Pool:

    100 Connections

Ab 200 requests aayi.

Flow:

    Request
        ↓
    Tomcat Thread
        ↓
    Business Logic
        ↓
    DB Query

Ab maan lo Database bahut slow hai.


## POSSIBLE REASONS WHY THE DATABASE BECOMES SLOW :
---------------------------------------------------

1. Slow Query
----------------
Query inefficient likhi gayi ho sakti hai.

Example:

    - Unnecessary joins
    - Large table scan
    - Poor query design

Result:

Ek query jo normally 20 ms me complete honi chahiye,
wo 5–10 seconds tak le sakti hai.



2. MISSING INDEX
------------------
Suppose query:

    SELECT * FROM orders
    WHERE customer_id = 101;

Agar customer_id column par index nahi hai,
to database ko poori table scan karni pad sakti hai.

Large tables me is wajah se query execution bahut slow ho sakta hai.



3. DATABASE LOCK CONTENTION
----------------------------

Sabse pehle samajhte hain ki Transaction kya hota hai.

## WHAT IS TRANSACTION ?
-------------------------

Transaction database operations ka ek logical group hota hai
jo ek single unit ki tarah execute hota hai.

Simple language me:

"Jo related database operations hum ek saath perform karna
chahte hain aur chahte hain ki ya to sab successful hon,
ya agar koi problem aaye to sab rollback ho jayein."

Example:

Suppose Anand ke account se ₹500 deduct karke
Anurag ke account me ₹500 add karna hai.

Ye do database operations hain:

Step-1

    Anand Account

    Balance = Balance - 500

Step-2

    Anurag Account

    Balance = Balance + 500

Ab socho agar pehla step successful ho gaya
aur server crash ho gaya.

Result:

✔ Anand ke account se paise kat gaye.

❌ Anurag ke account me paise aaye hi nahi.

Ye incorrect state hai.

Isliye dono operations ko ek Transaction ke andar execute
kiya jata hai.

Agar dono successful hue:

    COMMIT

Agar beech me koi error aa gaya:

    ROLLBACK

Yaani database pehle wali state me wapas chala jayega.


## EXAMPLE :
------------

Suppose Transaction-1 account id = 101 ko update kar rahi hai.

Transaction-1

    BEGIN;

    UPDATE account
    SET balance = balance - 500
    WHERE id = 101;

Database ne account id = 101 wali row par lock laga diya hai.

Abhi Transaction-1 complete nahi hui hai.


Isi beech Transaction-2 bhi same account ko update karna
chahti hai.

Transaction-2

    UPDATE account
    SET balance = balance + 100
    WHERE id = 101;

Ab Database kya karega?

Database Transaction-2 ko immediately execute nahi karega.

Use Transaction-1 ke COMMIT ya ROLLBACK hone ka wait karna padega.

Yahi waiting Database Lock Contention kehlati hai.

Result:

    Transaction-2 waiting state me chali jaati hai.

Agar bahut saari transactions same row ke lock ka wait
karne lagen,

to:

    Queries slow ho jaati hain.
            ↓
    Database Response Time increase ho jata hai.
            ↓
    Application slow feel hone lagti hai.


## DEFINITION :
----------------

Lock Contention occurs when multiple threads compete for the same lock. 
If one thread holds the lock for a long time, the remaining threads are blocked until the lock is released. 
This increases response time and can make the application slow even when CPU utilization is relatively low.


4. Too Many Concurrent Queries
--------------------------------
Database ek limited number of queries efficiently process
kar sakta hai.

Agar ek hi time par bahut zyada queries aa jayein,
to database sab queries immediately process nahi kar paata.

Result:

Queries queue me wait karti hain aur response time badh jata hai.



5. CPU SATURATION ON DATABASE SERVER
------------------------------------

(This applies when the database is deployed on a separate server.)

Suppose Database Server ka CPU continuously high utilization par chal raha hai.

Is wajah se Database ko queries execute karne me zyada time lagne lagta hai.

Result:

    Query Execution Time increase ho jata hai.

Aur kyunki application database ke response ka wait karti hai,

Overall Application Response Time bhi increase ho jata hai.


6. MEMORY PRESSURE
--------------------
Database frequently accessed data ko RAM me cache karta hai.

Agar available memory kam pad jaye,
to database ko data disk se read karna padta hai,
jo RAM ke comparison me kaafi slow hota hai.

Result:

Query execution time increase ho jata hai.



7. DISK I/O BOTTLENECK
------------------------
Database continuously disk par read/write operations karta hai.

Agar disk already busy ho ya slow ho,
to queries ko required data read/write karne me
extra time lagta hai.

Result:

Database slow ho jata hai.



8. NETWORK LATENCY BETWEEN APPLICATION AND DATABASE
------------------------------------------------------
Application aur Database alag machines par ho sakte hain.

Agar network slow hai ya latency high hai,
to request aur response travel karne me hi
extra time lag sakta hai.

Result:

Application ko database slow feel hota hai.



9. CONNECTION LEAK
--------------------
Application database connection lekar use properly
close / release nahi karti.

Result:

Connection Pool ki available connections gradually
kam hoti jaati hain.

Eventually Connection Pool Exhaust ho sakta hai,
aur naye requests ko connection available hone ka
wait karna padta hai.


Suppose ek query ko

    10 Seconds

lag rahe hain.

Ab kya hoga?

Pehli 100 requests ko DB connection mil gaya.

Lekin kyunki query bahut slow hai, ye 100 connections
10 seconds tak occupied rahenge.

Baaki 100 requests ko DB connection nahi milega.

Wo DB connection available hone ka wait karengi.

Diagram:

    200 Tomcat Threads

            ↓

    100 Threads
    Waiting for Slow DB Response

            ↓

    100 Threads
    Waiting for DB Connection

Question:

CPU kya kar raha hai?

Almost kuch nahi.

Kyun?

Kyunki threads computation nahi kar rahe.

Wo sirf DB response ya DB connection ka wait kar rahe hain.

CPU Utilization:

    20%

DB Connection Pool:

    100% Busy

Application:

    Very Slow

IMPORTANT:

Yahan primary root cause

    Slow Database / Slow Query

hai.

DB Connection Pool ka full ho jana actual root cause nahi hai.

Ye us slow database ka consequence (symptom) hai.


## INTERVIEW TIP :
------------------

Agar interviewer bole:

    "DB Connection Pool 100% busy hai."

To immediately ye conclude mat karna ki connection pool size kam hai.

Connection Pool Exhaustion aksar ek symptom hota hai.

Actual root cause investigate karna chahiye, jaise:

    - Slow Queries
    - Missing Indexes
    - Lock Contention
    - Connection Leaks
    - Network Latency

Production me pehle root cause identify kiya jata hai,
sirf connection pool size increase nahi kiya jata.



