Q3. WHAT METRICS WOULD YOU MONITOR BEFORE DECIDING TO SCALE?
--------------------------------------------------------------

1. CPU UTILIZATION
-------------------
Ye batata hai CPU kitna busy hai.
Agar continuously bahut high (e.g. 90-100%) ho, to CPU bottleneck ho sakta hai.


2. MEMORY USAGE
----------------
Ye batata hai application/server kitni RAM use kar raha hai.
Agar memory frequently fill hone lage, to JVM ko baar-baar Garbage Collection (GC) run karna padta hai.
GC ke kuch phases me application threads temporarily pause ho sakte hain, jisse response time increase ho sakta hai.
Aur agar memory fir bhi insufficient ho jaye, to application OutOfMemoryError throw kar sakti hai.


3. THREAD POOL USAGE
---------------------
Ye batata hai kitne worker threads currently busy hain.
Agar saare threads busy ho gaye, to naye requests wait ya reject ho sakte hain.


4. DATABASE CONNECTION POOL USAGE
----------------------------------
Ye batata hai connection pool me kitne DB connections use ho rahe hain.
Agar saare connections busy ho gaye, to requests connection ke liye wait karengi.


5. DATABASE CPU UTILIZATION
----------------------------
Ye batata hai Database Server ka CPU kitna busy hai.
High CPU indicate kar sakta hai ki database heavy load handle kar raha hai.


6. DATABASE DISK I/O
---------------------
Ye batata hai database kitna fast disk read/write kar pa raha hai.
High Disk I/O database ko slow bana sakta hai.


7. NETWORK UTILIZATION
-----------------------
Ye batata hai available network bandwidth ka kitna use ho raha hai.
Agar bandwidth limit ke paas pahunch gayi, to latency increase ho sakti hai.


8. REQUEST RATE (RPS)
----------------------
RPS (Requests Per Second) batata hai ek second me kitni requests aa rahi hain.
Traffic increase ho raha hai ya nahi, ye samajhne me help karta hai.


9. RESPONSE TIME
-----------------
Ek request ko complete hone me kitna time lag raha hai.
Agar response time badh raha hai, to system slow ho raha hai.


10. P95 LATENCY
----------------
95% requests kitne time ke andar complete ho rahi hain.
Ye average se better picture deta hai.


11. P99 LATENCY
----------------
99% requests kitne time ke andar complete ho rahi hain.
Worst-case user experience ko samajhne ke liye use hota hai.


12. QUEUE LENGTH
-----------------
Ye batata hai kitni incoming requests processing start hone ka wait kar rahi hain (i.e. worker thread available hone ka wait).
Agar queue continuously badh rahi ho, to application incoming requests ko utni fast process nahi kar pa rahi jitni fast requests aa rahi hain.


13. ERROR RATE
---------------
Kitni requests fail ho rahi hain (4xx/5xx etc.).
Error rate increase hona system health ke liye warning sign hai.


NOTE:
-----

Ye metrics generally Monitoring Dashboards me monitor kiye jaate hain.

Examples:

- Prometheus + Grafana (Most Common)
- AWS CloudWatch
- Datadog
- New Relic



