Application HttpSession create karne ke liye
Servlet Container (e.g. Tomcat) ka use karti hai.

Servlet Container (Tomcat) actual HttpSession object
create karta hai and user ki session-related
information store karta hai.

By default, ye HttpSession server ki local
memory (RAM) me store hota hai.

Uske baad Tomcat browser ko response ke saath
ek cookie bhejta hai.

Cookie me poora session data nahi bheja jata. 
Sirf Session ID bheji jaati hai.

Example:

    JSESSIONID = ABC123XYZ

Browser is cookie ko store kar leta hai.

Jab browser next request bhejta hai,

to browser automatically

    JSESSIONID = ABC123

Server ko bhej deta hai.

Tomcat apne Session Store me Session ID ko lookup
karta hai aur corresponding HttpSession Object
retrieve karta hai.

Uske baad application user ke Roles / Permissions
ke basis par Authorization perform kar sakti hai.

Isi wajah se user ko har request par dobara
login karne ki zarurat nahi padti.


